From: Magnesium maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] symbol_why: skip directories when scanning Kconfig files

The recursive glob also matches directories such as Kconfiglib in the
CVITEK kernel tree. Opening these as files raises IsADirectoryError and
aborts do_kernel_configcheck before the configuration can be audited.
Only scan regular files, retaining the normal configuration audit.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/tools/symbol_why.py
+++ b/tools/symbol_why.py
@@ -899,6 +899,8 @@
 kconfigs = glob.glob( ksrc + "/**/Kconfig*", recursive=True )
 all_configs = []
 for k in kconfigs:
+    if not os.path.isfile(k):
+        continue
     with open( k ) as kconfig_file:
         for kline in kconfig_file:
             m = re.match( r"^(menu).*config (\w*)", kline )
